    {
      "name": "reason_probability",
      "prompt_tokens": 47,
      "prompt_sha256": "21d30558472d17c8569e00c108f7c85038fee16ecf585bb86fbf06681f3e60af",
      "text": "To find the probability that both rolls are 6 given that at least one roll is 6, we use the definition of conditional probability:\n\n$$ P(A | B) = \\frac{P(A \\cap B)}{P(B)} $$\n\nLet $A$ be the event that both rolls are 6.\nLet $B$ be the event that at least one roll is 6.\n\n**Step 1: Determine the total number of outcomes.**\nA fair six-sided die is rolled twice. The total number of possible outcomes is:\n$$ 6 \\times 6 = 36 $$\n\n**Step 2: Determine the number of outcomes for event $B$ (at least one 6).**\nIt is easier to calculate the complement: the number of outcomes where *neither* roll is 6.\nIf neither roll is 6, each roll can be $\\{1, 2, 3, 4, 5\\}$, which gives 5 options per roll.\nNumber of outcomes with no 6s = $5 \\times 5 = 25$.\n\nTherefore, the number of outcomes with at least one 6 is:\n$$ 36 - 25 = 11 $$\nSo, $P(B) = \\frac{11}{36}$.\n\nAlternatively, we can list the 11 outcomes:\n$(6,1), (6,2), (6,3), (6,4), (6,5), (6,6)$\n$(1,6), (2,6), (3,6), (4,6), (5,6)$\n\n**Step 3: Determine the number of outcomes for event $A \\cap B$ (both rolls are 6 AND at least one is 6).**\nIf both rolls are 6, then obviously at least one roll is 6. So $A \\cap B$ is simply the event that both rolls are 6.\nThe only outcome is $(6,6)$.\nNumber of outcomes = 1.\nSo, $P(A \\cap B) = \\frac{1}{36}$.\n\n**Step 4: Calculate the conditional probability.**\n$$ P(A | B) = \\frac{P(A \\cap B)}{P(B)} = \\frac{1/36}{11/36} = \\frac{1}{11} $$\n\n1/11",
